```bash
cat > /tmp/fw.nft <<'EOF'
table inet demo {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;
    iif "lo" accept
    ct state established,related accept
    ip saddr 192.168.50.0/24 tcp dport 22 accept
    tcp dport 443 accept
  }
}
EOF
```
`inet` covers both IPv4 and IPv6. The `hook input` chain sees packets addressed to this host.

